:''This article is about the Cat Unit. For the enemy unit, see [[HI-DO (Enemy)]].''
'''HI-DO''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that was added in [[Version 4.3 Update|Version 4.3]] and can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Metal Slug Collaboration Event]]. [[True Form]] added in [[Version 13.1 Update|Version 13.1]] of [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]] and [[Version 13.7 Update|Version 13.7]] of [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]] increases health and attack, and decreases cost.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 225
|rarity = UR
|name1 = HI-DO
|name2 = HI-DO CC
|name3 = HI-DO MK III
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''HI-DO CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''HI-DO MK III''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
HI-DO is a great anti-Floating specialist unit. It has '''180,625''' health against floating and '''53,275''' damage against floating at just level 30 (if you include [[Fruit Treasures]]). Along with its naturally high range, this makes it an absolute beast against floating, though watch out for its ridiculously high cost. It is worth noting that as an anti-Floating unit, there are numerous options that may work better for either damage or crowd-controlling, though, such as [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Windy]] or [[Megidora (Uber Rare Cat)|Megidora]] respectively.

==='''True Form'''===
HI-DO's True Form lets it set itself apart from the competition with a nearly halved cost and even further boosted stats. While still somewhat outclassed by other options, it can at least be sent out much quicker due to the lowered cost.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Backliner}}

